 "author": "C07",
 "subject": "QA-07 entry side (left/right) and QA-09 reappearance (yes): the two branches that had never reached a candidate through the ordinary planning entry point.",
 "what_this_file_is": "A record of which pixel-visibility branches now reach a screened camera candidate, on which rooms, under which conditions, and with what was independently re-measured. It is planning evidence. It is not a QA item, not a dataset sample, and not pixel truth.",
 "claim_boundary": "Every row is a CPU screened candidate. No pixel was rendered for any of them: native visual 0, native audio 0, RLR 0, new query 0. A 'consistent' verdict means the projection-and-ray screen could not refute the requirement and the candidate is worth a render. A 'undetermined' verdict means even that much is not claimed - and every QA-09 occlusion screen comes back undetermined by construction, because the screening geometry is the room's acoustic proxy mesh and a projection screen can only ever refute a full occlusion, never confirm one. avengine.rooms.conditioned_visibility.accept_native_visibility on the renderer's own pixel truth remains the only authority that can pass any of these.",
 "why_they_used_to_fail": "Not search budget. Every retry of every failing request drew a still scene, so a fixed camera could never produce an out_of_view->visible crossing or a fully_occluded->visible transition. conditioned_visibility already reported that correctly, but only after the routes had been drawn. See CLAUDE_ROUND4_COORD/C07_TO_C01.json for the measurement and the patch.",
 "source_state": "conditioned_sampler.py was edited by its owner at 18:17 local and released at 18:28 (CLAUDE_ROUND4_COORD/C01_DONE.json), straddling this measurement. The three hm3d branches were rerun baseline-and-patched against the settled source and reproduced every number exactly (<attempt_dir>/final_base, <attempt_dir>/final_fix, fingerprint in <attempt_dir>/SOURCE_STATE_final.txt). The plans linked below are the earlier run of the same code path; their state series were re-derived independently, see independent_recheck.",
 "depends_on_an_unlanded_patch": "The 'after' column and every screened candidate below were produced with the conditioned_sampler.py patch in CLAUDE_ROUND4_COORD/C07_TO_C01.json loaded as a shadow module. That file belongs to C01 and was not modified on disk. Until C01 lands it, these branches still do not plan through the checked-in tree.",
